# Make it Live — Production Deployment

When the user says **"Make it Live"** (any casing), deploy the latest `main` branch to **web.nutrifreaks.com** without asking for confirmation unless credentials are missing.

## Steps

1. Ensure changes are committed and pushed to `origin/main`.
2. Run: `python scripts/deploy-live.py` from the project root (requires `all` permissions).
3. Confirm exit code `0` and output contains `DEPLOY_OK`.
4. Briefly report success and link https://web.nutrifreaks.com

## Server details

| Item | Value |
|------|-------|
| Host | `72.61.224.223` |
| User | `root` |
| App dir | `/var/www/web.nutrifreaks.com` |
| PM2 app | `nutrifreaks-web` |
| Repo | `https://github.com/nutrifreaksindia-png/nutrifreaks-website.git` |

## Credentials

Read from `.deploy.env` (gitignored). If missing, ask the user for SSH host/user/password — never commit credentials.

## Deploy flow (automated by script)

Clone to `/tmp/nutrifreaks-website-deploy` → `npm install` → `npm run build` → rsync standalone output to app dir → copy static + public → `pm2 restart nutrifreaks-web`

**Important:** Use `npm install` (not `npm ci` with `NODE_ENV=production`) so devDependencies like TypeScript are available for the build.
